---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../config';
const updated = 'July 25, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy | Balance Bridge Financial" description="How Balance Bridge Financial collects, uses, and protects your information." noIndex={false}>
  <section class="bg-navy py-14"><div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-white">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] text-steel-400">Last updated: {updated}</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
    <div class="prose-bb">
      <p><strong>Plain-English summary:</strong> we collect only what we need to respond to you and to provide bookkeeping services, we protect it carefully, and we never sell it. This policy is a solid baseline and should be reviewed by an attorney before you rely on it. <!-- PLACEHOLDER: attorney review --></p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>{BUSINESS.legalName} ("Balance Bridge," "we," "us") operates {BUSINESS.url} and the client portal at {BUSINESS.portalUrl}. Contact: {BUSINESS.email}.</p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact and inquiry data</strong> — name, email, phone, business details you submit through our forms or calendar bookings.</li>
        <li><strong>Client engagement data</strong> — financial records, statements, payroll data, and documents you provide through the client portal so we can perform the services you hire us for.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — standard server logs (IP address, browser type, pages requested) used for security and troubleshooting. Our public website does not use advertising trackers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>To respond to inquiries, deliver contracted services, send service communications, invoice and process payments (via Stripe — card details never touch our servers), meet legal obligations, and secure our systems. If you download a resource, we may send occasional relevant emails; every one includes an unsubscribe link.</p>

      <h2>How we protect it</h2>
      <p>Encryption in transit (TLS) on all sites; portal data encrypted at rest; role-based, least-privilege access; multi-factor authentication available on all portal accounts; audit logging of access to client files; and regular backups. No method is 100% secure, but we treat your financial data with the care we'd demand for our own.</p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>We never sell personal information. We share it only with: service providers under confidentiality obligations (hosting, payment processing, e-signature, email delivery); your designated third parties (e.g., your CPA, with your authorization); and authorities when legally required.</p>

      <h2>Retention & your choices</h2>
      <p>We retain engagement records for the period required by professional and tax record-keeping standards, then delete or anonymize them. You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information (subject to legal retention duties) by emailing {BUSINESS.email}.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>The public site uses only essential cookies and privacy-respecting analytics, if any. The client portal uses strictly necessary session cookies to keep you signed in.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Our services are for businesses and are not directed to children under 13; we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We'll post any updates here with a revised date. Material changes affecting portal users will be announced in the portal.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
